<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngwana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngwana was a leader of one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni-speaking</a> groups displaced during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. His forces crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> in the early 1820s. They were the first of several waves of raiders whose attacks contributed to the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a>.</p></div>
